---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Stats from "../../components/Stats.astro";
import { langs, t, path, type Lang } from "../../i18n/ui";
import { lessons, split } from "../../lib/lessons";
import summary from "../../data/summary.json";
export const getStaticPaths = () => langs.map((lang) => ({ params: { lang } }));
const lang = Astro.params.lang as Lang;
const learn = await lessons("learn", lang);
const read = await lessons("read", lang);
---
<Base lang={lang} active="home">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">RNA-seq · differential expression · publication-ready output</div>
        <h1>From your results table to figures you can submit</h1>
        <p class="lead">From an accession to a sample sheet and download scripts, to a DESeq2 script you run on your own computer, to significant genes, journal-size figures, legends and methods text. Your data never leave your machine.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={path(lang, "script")}>Generate a DESeq2 script</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={path(lang, "results")}>Explore your results</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art">
        <img src="/plots/volcano.png" alt="Volcano plot of the airway dataset: log2 fold change against adjusted p-value, with the strongest genes labelled" width="1800" height="1600" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Analysis tools</h2><p>Start from the output of your own differential-expression run.</p></div>
      <div class="grid">
        <a class="card" href={path(lang, "dataset")}>
          <span class="n">01</span>
          <h3>Dataset to sample sheet</h3>
          <p>Type a GEO, SRA or ENA accession. See every run with its metadata, reads and file size; build and download the sample sheet; get the FASTQ download scripts (bash, PowerShell, SRA Toolkit) and the fastp + Salmon quantification script.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={path(lang, "script")}>
          <span class="n">02</span>
          <h3>DESeq2 script generator</h3>
          <p>Describe your experiment (Salmon folders or a count matrix, sample sheet, condition, batch) and download a complete, commented R script or Colab notebook that runs tximport and DESeq2, writes the results tables and makes the standard plots. Tested on the airway data.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={path(lang, "results")}>
          <span class="n">03</span>
          <h3>Explore your results</h3>
          <p>Upload a results table, choose thresholds, and get: significant genes as CSV and Excel, volcano and MA plots as SVG and 300-dpi PNG at journal widths, figure legends, and a ZIP with everything plus an HTML report and the settings. Ensembl IDs are mapped to symbols automatically.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={path(lang, "enrich")}>
          <span class="n">04</span>
          <h3>Enrichment</h3>
          <p>GO, KEGG, Reactome and WikiPathways enrichment of your up- and down-regulated genes, with the genes you tested as the statistical background, through the g:Profiler service. Table with fold enrichment, a journal-size dot plot, CSV and a ready legend.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={path(lang, "hub")}>
          <span class="n">05</span>
          <h3>Hub genes</h3>
          <p>Upload the STRING network of your DEGs, rank nodes with the twelve cytoHubba scores (MCC, Degree, Betweenness…), choose the top N, and download the hub table, the network figure and SIF/attribute files that open in Cytoscape. Scores checked against networkx.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href={path(lang, "methods")}>
          <span class="n">06</span>
          <h3>Methods writer</h3>
          <p>Enter the tools, versions and settings you used (fastp, Salmon, tximport, DESeq2, apeglm, clusterProfiler) and get a methods paragraph with numbered, verified citations, plus a BibTeX file.</p>
        </a>
        <div class="card soon">
          <span class="n">07</span>
          <h3>More tools</h3>
          <p>Sensitivity analysis and multi-cohort comparison are next. The list grows as the author's own analyses need them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Tested on real data</h2><p>Every tool is checked against a complete analysis of a public dataset, whose numbers are shown throughout the site.</p></div>
      <Stats items={[
        { value: 8, label: "airway samples (Himes et al. 2014)" },
        { value: summary.genes_tested, label: "genes tested" },
        { value: summary.sig_005, label: "changed at adjusted p below 0.05" },
        { value: summary.sig_005_lfc1, label: "of those, more than two-fold" },
      ]} />
      <p class="muted">Inputs, versions, downloads and a check against the original paper are on the <a href={path(lang, "data")}>data and methods page</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section learn-strip">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>If you want to understand what the tools do</h2><p>A course that follows the airway dataset from raw reads to pathways, and a guide to reading every kind of plot.</p></div>
      <div class="two">
        <div>
          <h3 class="strip-h"><a href={path(lang, "learn")}>{t(lang, "learn.title")}</a> <span class="muted small">· {learn.length} lessons</span></h3>
          <ol class="mini">{learn.map((e) => <li><a href={path(lang, "learn", split(e.id).slug)}>{e.data.title}</a></li>)}</ol>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="strip-h"><a href={path(lang, "read")}>{t(lang, "read.title")}</a> <span class="muted small">· {read.length} pages</span></h3>
          <ol class="mini">{read.map((e) => <li><a href={path(lang, "read", split(e.id).slug)}>{e.data.title}</a></li>)}</ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <style>
    .card.soon { opacity: 0.75; cursor: default; }
    .card.soon:hover { transform: none; box-shadow: none; border-color: var(--line); }
    .learn-strip { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 2.5rem; }
    .strip-h { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
    .strip-h a { text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink); }
    .mini { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.4rem; font-size: 0.93rem; line-height: 1.5; }
    .mini li { margin: 0.25em 0; }
    .mini a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
    .mini a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  </style>
</Base>
